# Test: an operator SPD entry the dataplane refuses never commits quietly. At the
# start it is logged at Error and the rest of the IPsec block installs; on a reload
# the refusal refuses the reload.
# Spec: spec-rfc4301-architecture-gaps (AC-14, RFC 4301
#       Section 4.4.1, the SPD management interface; owner decision 2026-11-19,
#       "Install, log, doctor").
#
# QUESTION: when the dataplane refuses a `vpn ipsec policy` entry, does the operator
# learn it from the operation they ran, the start or the reload, with the entry's
# name and the dataplane's answer? The unit tests
# (engine/rfc4301_spd_install_failure_test.go) prove the reconcilers and that the
# dataplane keeps the previous form; only this test proves the refusal reaches the
# operator through the daemon's own start and its SIGHUP reload pipeline (config
# file, the ike plugin's verify, then its apply, applyConfig -> installSPDPolicies).
#
# VALIDATES:
#   - the start config holds `drop` (discard, order 900) and `held` (bypass,
#     order 4242, disjoint prefixes). The backend refuses `held`: the start logs
#     "Ze could not install operator SPD policy held" at Error and does not stop;
#   - the reload moves `drop` to order 4242 and removes `held`. It passes verify (one
#     entry, nothing to tie with) and its apply is refused: the reload error names
#     `drop` and carries the backend's answer, and the reload is never reported
#     complete.
# PREVENTS: the D-1 defect, where installSPDPolicies logged the refusal at Warn and
#   the reload was reported complete while the operator's discard entry was not in
#   force.
#
# WHY A TEST BACKEND. No refusal of the kernel's is reachable from an operator
# configuration the commit verifier accepts: every EINVAL of verify_newpolicy_info
# (net/xfrm/xfrm_user.c) judges a field the verifier already holds to the same rule
# (selector family and prefix lengths, action, direction), an operator entry carries
# no template for validate_tmpl to judge, and the XFRM backend's update form never
# meets the EEXIST of an exclusive insert. The zetest-only recording-spd-refused
# backend (internal/component/ike/dataplane/recording_spd_refused_zetest.go) refuses
# an operator entry at order 4242 and records every other write, so the test runs
# unprivileged. That a discard entry reaches the REAL kernel as action discard is
# test/ipsec/ipsec-spd-order-readback.ci.
#
# NOT HERE: AC-19's half of this test waits on D-6.
#
# RED PROOF: in internal/component/ike/engine/spd_policy.go installSPDPolicies,
#   replace `return spdInstallRefusal(...)` with `return nil` (the D-1 shape): the
#   reload is reported complete and no reload error is printed, red. In
#   installSPDPoliciesAtStart, drop the log.LogAttrs line: the start assertion is red.

option=env:var=ze_test_ike_dataplane:value=recording-spd-refused
option=env:var=ze_test_ike_port:value=$PORT2
option=env:var=ze_log_ike:value=info
option=timeout:value=30s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy drop {
			action discard
			order 900
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 198.18.252.0/24
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.253.0/24
			}
		}
		policy held {
			action bypass
			order 4242
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 198.18.254.0/24
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.255.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy drop {
			action discard
			order 4242
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 198.18.252.0/24
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.253.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=25s

await=stderr:contains=reload error:then=stop
expect=stderr:contains=Ze could not install operator SPD policy held
expect=stderr:contains=Ze could not install operator SPD policy drop
expect=stderr:contains=the recording-spd-refused test backend refuses an operator SPD entry at order 4242
reject=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
